.\" scp(1) for Amix: the scp of Dropbear 2026.94 (from OpenSSH's, BSD
.\" licence, see /opt/amix/doc/dropbear/LICENSE).  Written for this package.
.TH SCP 1 "1 November 2026" "dropbear 2026.94"
.SH NAME
scp \- copy files over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scp
[
.B \-prqv
] [
.B \-P
.I port
] [
.B \-i
.I keyfile
] [
.B \-l
.I limit
] [
.B \-S
.I program
]
\fIsource\fP ... \fItarget\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scp
copies files between hosts.
A remote file is written
[\fIuser\fP@]\fIhost\fP:\fIpath\fP;
a path without a host is a local file.
The connection is made by
.BR dbclient (1),
which asks for a password or uses a key as it always does, and the
remote host runs
.B scp
too.
.TP
.B \-p
Keep the files' times and modes.
.TP
.B \-r
Copy directories and what they hold.
.TP
.B \-q
Show no progress.
.TP
.B \-v
Have
.B dbclient
say what it does.
.TP
.BI \-P " port"
The remote port.
.TP
.BI \-i " keyfile"
The key to log in with (see
.BR dbclient (1)).
.TP
.BI \-l " limit"
Use at most
.I limit
Kbit/s, a whole number.
.TP
.BI \-S " program"
Connect with
.I program
instead of
.BR /opt/amix/bin/dbclient .
.TP
.BI \-o " option"
An option for
.BR dbclient ,
as its
.B \-o
takes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.ft CW
$ scp notes.txt user@server:/tmp
$ scp -r user@server:src .
.ft R
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dbclient (1),
.BR dropbear (8)
.SH NOTES
This is the original scp protocol.
From another system with OpenSSH 9.0 or later, whose
.B scp
uses SFTP unless told otherwise, copy to and from this system with
.BR "scp \-O" .
File times are kept to the second.
